# Package Gate Example

Copy this file to `.agent/package_gate.md` only for local runs. The live file is
ignored and must not be committed.

When a new package starts, refresh the live gate so the active package and unit
match the current approved work. Stale active-package references are a stop
condition.

## Package

Package 10 - Deterministic GTM policy layer

## Active unit

Set this manually for one approved Package 10 unit:

1. Package 10A - Docs-first deterministic GTM policy contract
2. Package 10B - Input validation and policy matrix helpers
3. Package 10C - Policy table build and safe context join
4. Package 10D - Audit, idempotence, and optional observability context
5. Package 10E - CLI, Make targets, local export, and docs closeout

## Package-level exit gate

Package 10 is complete only when:

- `docs/gtm_policy.md` remains the source of truth.
- `gtm_policy_v1` is implemented exactly as documented.
- `mart.account_month_gtm_policy` exists at one row per `account_id` x
  `scoring_month`.
- Raw churn and expansion scores remain separate preserved columns.
- High churn risk dominates expansion actioning.
- High churn plus high expansion resolves to save-first behaviour.
- Invalid scores fail before assignment.
- Every valid score row maps to exactly one policy row.
- `metadata.gtm_policy_audit` is append-only.
- Reruns replace policy rows only for the selected scoring month.
- Optional Package 9 observability context, if used, is recorded honestly
  without changing the deterministic matrix.
- Local exports remain generated ignored artefacts.
- Package 10 does not add labels, learned policy, dashboards, APIs, cloud
  services, CRM execution, broad final polish, or commercial-validation claims.
- `make verify` passes.
- `git diff --check` passes.
- Public repo safety check passes.
- No generated outputs, DuckDB files, MLflow runs, cache folders, live `.agent`
  files, private files, or local-only artefacts are tracked.

## Package 10A exit gate

Package 10A is complete only when:

- `docs/gtm_policy.md` defines the deterministic v1 contract, exact matrix,
  taxonomy, conflict handling, boundaries, audit/idempotence, CLI/Make contract,
  tests, review checklist, and deferred Package 11 items.
- `docs/packages.md`, `docs/runbook.md`, `docs/decisions.md`, and `README.md`
  align with the narrowed Package 10 scope.
- Committed `.agent/*.example` templates reference Package 10 and the approved
  10A-10E unit structure.
- No code, scripts, tests, Make targets, generated outputs, DuckDB tables, or
  exports are added.
- Live local `.agent/*.md` files remain ignored and untracked.
- `make public-safety-check` passes.
- `git diff --check` passes.

## Stop conditions

Stop before making any change that would:

- Change the locked `gtm_policy_v1` matrix, thresholds, exact strings, or
  boundary rules without an explicit durable-doc decision/update.
- Mutate Package 8 raw score rows or scoring audit evidence.
- Mutate Package 9 observability outputs.
- Use labels or future outcomes.
- Use real customer or company data.
- Add learned policy, optimization, reinforcement learning, or automatic
  actioning.
- Add dashboards, APIs, cloud deployment, CRM integration, campaign execution,
  email automation, or playbook engines.
- Claim real-world commercial validation from synthetic outputs.
- Add broad final-polish work that belongs to Package 11.
- Weaken public-repo security.
- Commit generated artefacts.
- Commit live local `.agent/*.md` files.
- Add unapproved production dependencies.
- Remove or weaken tests.
- Expand Package 10 beyond the approved 10A-10E slices.
